.TH LOGLENS 1 "October 2026" "v1.0.0" "LogLens AI Manual"
.SH NAME
loglens \- Autonomous Linux Systems Administrator and Security Copilot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loglens
[\fI"QUERY"\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loglens
is a terminal-based AI assistant powered by Google Gemma/Gemini models. It automatically scans host system telemetry (OS, architecture, package managers) and generates tailored, natively executable Bash commands to resolve system administration and security auditing tasks.
.PP
LogLens operates with a human-in-the-loop safeguard, proposing the exact command and awaiting user confirmation before executing on the host system.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB"QUERY"\fR
The natural language task or error message you want LogLens to resolve. Must be enclosed in quotes if it contains spaces.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Install a package from the standard repositories or AUR:
$ loglens "install feroxbuster"
.TP
Troubleshoot a systemd service:
$ loglens "check why docker.service is failing to start"
.TP
Perform network and port diagnostics:
$ loglens "find whatever is running on port 8080 and kill it"
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GEMINI_API_KEY
Required. The API key for authenticating with Google GenAI endpoints. Can be exported in the shell or stored in a \fB.env\fR file in the project directory.
.SH AUTHOR
Built for Hacktoberfest Hack Day Pune x Poona College.
